/* ============================================================================
   birthday-simulation.epher -- 5000 groups of 23: how many share a day

   Fill rooms of 23 people with birthdays drawn uniformly from 365 days
   and count the rooms where at least two people share a birthday. The
   theoretical rate is the birthday-problem answer, 0.507297234324, so
   about half of all 23-person rooms collide; with 5000 rooms the
   standard error is about 0.007 and the seeded run below (randseed(19))
   should land within 0.02 of the theory.

   One room is simulated exactly: birthdays are drawn one at a time and
   the draw collides with probability (distinct days seen) / 365, which
   is exact by symmetry; the first collision ends the room. A recursion
   of depth at most 23 plays the room, and the packed loop replays it
   5000 times. The stream is reproducible, so every run of this file
   prints the same rate.

   Source: the birthday problem of Feller, volume 1, chapter 2, played
   as a simulation.

   Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/probability/simulations/birthday-simulation.epher"
   Web/desktop:             paste the file into the entry, press Enter

   The knobs to edit are `rooms` and `size`; everything below them is
   machinery.
   ============================================================================ */

// ---- the knobs ----
const rooms = 5000
const size = 23

// ---- helpers ----
def fill(k, d) = if k == size then 0 else if randint(1, 365) <= d then 1 else fill(k + 1, d + 1)
/* fill(k, d): k birthdays drawn so far, d of them distinct. The next
   draw collides with probability d/365 (the distinct days may be
   relabelled 1..d), so the room returns 1 on the first collision and 0
   if all `size` birthdays are distinct. Exact simulation, no pruning. */

// ---- results ----
// The 5000 rooms, seeded: one shared-birthday flag per room, totalled.
randseed(19)
v = {0, 0}
while v[1] < rooms do v = {v[1] + 1, v[2] + fill(1, 1)}

// The empirical rate against the exact theory of the companion script
// probability/counting/birthday-problem.epher: 1 - prod(1 - k/365).
print("rooms:", rooms)
print("rooms with a shared birthday:", v[2])
print("empirical rate:", v[2] / rooms)
w = {1, 1}
while w[1] < size do w = {w[1] + 1, w[2] * (1 - w[1] / 365)}
print("theoretical rate:", 1 - w[2])
print("difference:", v[2] / rooms - (1 - w[2]))
/* ---- expected output ----
= 5000
= 23
= 19
= {0, 0}
= rooms: 5000
= rooms with a shared birthday: 2526
= empirical rate: 0.5052
= {1, 1}
= theoretical rate: 0.507297234324
= difference: -0.00209723432399
*/
